      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A big issue here is differentiating between a package that was only installed as a dependency vs a package that the user actually wants to keep installed.\nE.g. suppose packages A, B, C and D are installed, with each package being dependent on the previous package [A<-B<-C<-D].\nPackages A and C aren't directly useful to the user, but are requirements for packages B and D respectively.\nAfter some time and consideration, the user concludes that package D is no longer needed, and moves to uninstall it.\nThe user still wishes to keep B installed though. How is VPM supposed to know to remove C, but to keep B?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
