      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e4ca2145f9b3726b3b389e7|full_name}: I see two other solutions:\n1. have a flag in the package.json that tells VPM whether or not the package provides user functionality on its own. If it does not, VPM can safely remove it if no package depends on it.\n2. behave similar to apt in that VPM remembers if it was asked to install a package or if a package was installed as a dependency. And only the latter can be removed automatically.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
