  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm trying adding & removing User Package with some small test packages to know how VCC resolves dependencies, these days.\nWhen I added and removed a package with the following `package.json`, `\"com.anatawa12.custom-localization-for-editor-extension\"` will still exist in dependencies.\nI'm sorry if this will be fixed with unimplemented planned feature of VCC.\n**Steps to reproduce**\n1. Create empty folder & create ``package.json`` with the following json\n2. Add the created folder as user packages to Creator Companion.\n3. Select a project in CreatorCompanion\n4. Add 'UPM VPM Test' on User Packages tab\n5. Remove 'UPM VPM Test' on User Packages tab\n**Expected behavior**\n\"com.anatawa12.custom-localization-for-editor-extension\" does not exist in dependencies of project (`manifest.json`).\n**Actual behavior**\n\"com.anatawa12.custom-localization-for-editor-extension\" still exist in dependencies of project (`manifest.json`).\n**The `package.json` file**\n```\n{\n  \"name\": \"com.anatawa12.upm-vpm-test\",\n  \"displayName\": \"UPM VPM Test\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"gitDependencies\": {\n    \"com.anatawa12.custom-localization-for-editor-extension\": \"https://github.com/anatawa12/CustomLocalization4EditorExtension.git#0.1.2\"\n  }\n}\n```",
